1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
 When the internet stops, volunteer work usually does not.

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:09,940
 Relay Ledger keeps a small team's tasks moving without an account or a central server.

3
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:11,400
 This is the actual app.

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:14,420
 The example is a community repair day.

5
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:18,160
 Tasks have an owner, a status, and notes for the next person.

6
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:21,980
 I can create a fresh board and add a task in a few seconds.

7
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:24,600
 Each change is saved on this device.

8
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,080
 Now imagine two volunteers working separately.

9
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:32,280
 One marks the same task in progress, the other marks it done.

10
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:36,200
 A timestamp should not silently choose who is right.

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:39,580
 Relay Ledger exchanges the full update history.

12
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:43,840
 In exchange, I prepare an encrypted snapshot using a passphrase.

13
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:49,120
 I can save a handoff file or show a repeating stream of QR packets.

14
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:51,260
 The passphrase is shared separately.

15
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:53,720
 It is never inside the QR code.

16
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:57,120
 The other device collects the packets in any order.

17
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,880
 Duplicate frames are ignored.

18
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:03,560
 Missing frames stay visible, and nothing imports until the package is complete.

19
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:08,360
 A file is the fallback when a camera is slow or the board is large.

20
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,520
 Here I open the incoming handoff.

21
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:13,280
 A wrong passphrase fails safely.

22
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:16,760
 With the right one, I see a preview before merging.

23
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:19,180
 Both independent updates are preserved.

24
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:21,480
 The board asks for a decision.

25
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:26,680
 Choosing a status creates a new update that acknowledges both earlier versions.

26
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:31,680
 History keeps the context, and importing an older copy cannot erase the decision.

27
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:36,300
 The app can reopen offline after its first complete installation.

28
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:38,960
 Local workspace data is plain text.

29
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:41,600
 Handoff encryption is a separate boundary.

30
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,640
 Names are labels, not verified identities.

31
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:48,400
 Physical camera performance still needs device testing.

32
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:54,520
 Built for OFFGRID, Relay Ledger combines a causal event model, authenticated encryption,

33
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:58,080
 real QR decoding, and deliberate merge review.

34
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:00,040
 The code is open source.

35
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:04,320
 Our next step is testing these handoffs with small volunteer teams.

36
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:07,160
 Keep the work moving, even when the connection stops.

